From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sadatdaniel <sadatdaniel@yahoo.com>
Date: Thu, 4 Sep 2026 14:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: samsung: abox: resume synchronously so the DSP boots

No audio on this device: every PCM write fails with -EIO and the driver
logs "Invalid calliope state: 0" (CALLIOPE_DISABLED) forever.

samsung_abox_probe() does:

	pm_runtime_enable(dev);
	pm_runtime_set_autosuspend_delay(dev, 1);
	pm_runtime_use_autosuspend(dev);
	pm_runtime_get(dev);

pm_runtime_get() is asynchronous - it increments the usage count and
never invokes the resume callback. abox_runtime_resume() -> abox_enable()
is the only path that downloads calliope_sram.bin / calliope_dram.bin and
releases the audio DSP from reset, so the DSP is never started. Worse,
the usage count is then pinned, so the device can never idle and resume
later either: runtime_status stays "active" for the lifetime of the boot
while the DSP is still in reset.

Observed on a Galaxy A50 (exynos9610) running Ubuntu Touch:

  * runtime_status = active from boot, autosuspend_delay_ms = 1, but the
    device never suspends and abox_enable() never appears in dmesg;
  * no "abox_download_firmware" and no "SRAM firmware loaded" either;
  * speaker-test straight to hw:0,0, with PulseAudio stopped, fails with
    "Write error: -5,Input/output error";
  * the Android audio HAL is driven correctly through the whole userspace
    stack (logcat shows real adev_open_output_stream/out_write calls), so
    the fault is squarely below it.

Ruled out first: firmware presence (calliope_*.bin are installed and the
"Failed to request firmware" error is gone), the CP/cass daemon, ALSA
node permissions, and the calliope_cmd FAILSAFE path.

Use pm_runtime_get_sync() so the resume callback actually runs at probe.

NOT YET BOOT-TESTED - see README.md in this directory.
---
diff --git a/sound/soc/samsung/abox/abox.c b/sound/soc/samsung/abox/abox.c
index 0d900fb0b..3ed9c5a49 100644
--- a/sound/soc/samsung/abox/abox.c
+++ b/sound/soc/samsung/abox/abox.c
@@ -6304,7 +6304,17 @@ static int samsung_abox_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	pm_runtime_enable(dev);
 	pm_runtime_set_autosuspend_delay(dev, 1);
 	pm_runtime_use_autosuspend(dev);
-	pm_runtime_get(dev);
+	/*
+	 * pm_runtime_get() only increments the usage count; it never invokes
+	 * the resume callback. abox_runtime_resume() -> abox_enable() is the
+	 * only path that downloads the calliope firmware and releases the
+	 * audio DSP from reset, so with a plain get() the DSP is never
+	 * started - and because the usage count stays pinned the device can
+	 * never idle and resume later either. The result is calliope_state
+	 * stuck at CALLIOPE_DISABLED ("Invalid calliope state: 0") and every
+	 * PCM write failing with -EIO. Resume synchronously instead.
+	 */
+	pm_runtime_get_sync(dev);
 
 	data->qos_nb.notifier_call = abox_qos_notifier;
 	pm_qos_add_notifier(PM_QOS_AUD_THROUGHPUT, &data->qos_nb);
--
